      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3b9d61fc-79e3-59bb-9e63-0a0a717e7e51",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Eleutherococcus, Amaryllis, Chengiopanax sciadophylloides, Hippeastrum puniceum\n- Taxonomy: genus, species, subtribe, tribe, family Araliaceae, Amaryllidinae, Amaryllideae\n\nFacts:\n- Eleutherococcus is a genus of 38 species of thorny shrubs and trees in the family Araliaceae.\n- Amaryllis is the only genus in the subtribe Amaryllidinae of the tribe Amaryllideae.\n- Chengiopanax sciadophylloides was previously included in the genus Eleutherococcus.\n- Chengiopanax sciadophylloides is distinguished from Eleutherococcus by lacking spines or prickles.\n- ITS sequence data confirmed the separation of Chengiopanax sciadophylloides from Eleutherococcus.\n- Hippeastrum puniceum is commonly called Barbados lily, Easter lily, cacao lily, cocoa lily, and amaryllis lily.\n- Hippeastrum puniceum is neither a true lily nor a species of Amaryllis.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
