        "original_id": "1905ce07-73b2-5fbd-a14d-03c17281e058",
        "text": "Page: Eleutherococcus. Sentence: Eleutherococcus is a genus of 38 species of thorny shrubs and trees in the family Araliaceae.\nPage: Amaryllis. Sentence: Amaryllis ( ) is the only genus in the subtribe Amaryllidinae (tribe Amaryllideae).\nPage: Chengiopanax sciadophylloides. Sentence: Previously included in the genus \"Eleutherococcus\", it is distinguished from other members of that genus by not having spines or prickles and ITS sequence data confirmed the separation.\nPage: Hippeastrum puniceum. Sentence: Common names include Barbados lily, Easter lily, cacao lily, cocoa lily and amaryllis lily, although it is neither a lily nor a species of \"Amaryllis\".",
